# research/results — commit the record, never the artifacts.
#
# Per research-loop conventions.md § Version Control: run.json, config.yaml,
# metrics.json, notes.md, stdout.log and trajectory.json are small, diffable,
# and the entire point — they get committed. Checkpoints, plots and large
# outputs do not.
#
# This file also keeps the otherwise-empty results/ directory in git. Paths are
# relative to this directory.
#
# If stdout.log is enormous, truncate the middle and say so *in the file*
# rather than ignoring it.

**/artifacts/
*.ckpt
*.pt
*.safetensors
*.parquet
